" [:option {:value "255147"} "Kayak Relay, 4 × 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255191"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255203"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255209"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255221"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255007"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "255031"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "255059"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "255095"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "255240"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "255302"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "255366"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "255482"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255620"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255714"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255822"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255967"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256104"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256235"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256346"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258770"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "307048"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353482"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016138"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/163"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "26 – 29 August 1960"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/418"} "Lago Albano, Castel Gandolfo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/255133"} "46 from 23 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The reigning World Champions in the K-2 1000 were " [:a {:href ""} "Rik Verbrugghe"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9153"} "Germain Van De Moere"] ", while " [:a {:href "/athletes/10965"} "Yevhen Yatsynenko"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10961"} "Ivan Holovachov"] " of the Soviet Union were the most recent runners-up. Yatsynenko did not attend the 1960 Summer Olympics, but the other three were there and contenders for the podium, with Holovachov partnering with " [:a {:href "/athletes/11010"} "Mykolas Rudzinskas"] ". Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10080"} "György Mészáros"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10098"} "András Szente"] " were the reigning European champions and were also in contention. All of these pairs, however, would have to face the Swedish duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10803"} "Sven-Olov Sjödelius"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10762"} "Gert Fredriksson"] ", the latter of whom was a multiple Olympic and World Champion in other disciplines."] "\n\n" [:p {} "None of these nations, however, won their opening heats, which were taken by " [:a {:href "/athletes/10356"} "Ruud Knuppe"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10352"} "Toon Geurts"] " of the Netherlands, Danish brothers " [:a {:href "/athletes/9455"} "Kai"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9456"} "Vagn Schmidt"] ", and Germans " [:a {:href "/athletes/9834"} "Wolfgang Lange"] " and " [:a {:href ""} "Dieter Krause"] ". With different crews, Denmark had been the 1957 European runners-up, while Germany had been the 1957 and 1959 European champion and bronze medalist respectively. The semi-finals had results that were more expected, as the heats were taken by Hungary, the Soviet Union, and the Polish duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10538"} "Władysław Zieliński"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10487"} "Stefan Kapłaniak"] ". The only major upset was the elimination of Belgium in the first heat, in favor of Hungary, Sweden, and the Netherlands. The final came down to a race to the finish between Sweden and Hungary, which the former won by a margin of only 0.18 seconds, leaving the latter with silver and giving Fredriksson the rare distinction of having earned a gold medal at four consecutive Olympics. He was the first canoeist to accomplish this and his feat was not repeated until 1984, when " [:a {:href "/athletes/10605"} "Ivan Patzaichin"] "  of Romania won his fourth gold medal in the C-2 1000. Poland, meanwhile, took bronze by an ever smaller margin over the Soviet Union: 0.12 seconds. Mészáros and Szente won another silver medal at these Games as members of the K-1 4 x 500 metres relay crew."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10762"} "Gert Fredriksson"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10803"} "Sven-Olov Sjödelius"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "3:46.50 (3 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "3:47.64 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "3:34.73 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Best"} "OB"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10080"} "György Mészáros"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10098"} "András Szente"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "3:38.28 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "3:46.75 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:34.91 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [